                "text": "**Analyzing Grid Formats**\n\nI'm focusing on these vertically striped 1D grids, and mapping rows to 0 or C for their color. I'm exploring an example where I consolidate identical rows, as shown by the provided input and its corresponding output. I am starting to develop an algorithm to tackle the rearrangement.\n\n\n**Discovering Ordering Patterns**\n\nI've made a breakthrough. Examining run lengths of the colored segments (specifically '2' or '5', and then '7'), I've found a consistent pattern: the output's colored segments are sorted in descending order of their lengths. This seems crucial to the rearrangement algorithm. The 0s are staying put, too. I'm excited by this ordering.\n\n\n",
